Fair enough.  I can understand wanting to exclude Americanisms.  But within 
the US, 'any more' is only used as an adverb modifying an adjective or an 
adjective modifying a noun.  I never see it used as a time adverb 
meaning 'any longer'.  Americans use 'anymore' instead.

I thought it was as old and as standard as words like anything, anyone, 
something, sometime, etc, but clearly that's not the case.

